    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0244" n="238" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg238"/>

                <head>No. 16.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Carter to Mr. Foster</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington, D. C.</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-02-11"><hi rendition="#italic">February 11, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received February 11, 1893.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In response to your request for information
                    on the subjects of the resources of the ex-Queen and the Princess Kauilani, the
                    public lands, and the islands and dependencies of the Hawaiians, the inclosed
                    statements have been prepared from such sources of information as were available
                    to the commission, and are submitted for the use of your Department.</p>
                <p>With assurance of esteem,</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles L.
                    Carter.</hi></signed></closer>




